---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/videos.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Lacrima Videos"
  description="Privacy policy for Lacrima Videos CLI, the internal tool Lacrima Videos uses to publish to and analyze its own YouTube channels."
  canonical="https://lacrima.dev/videos/privacy/"
>
  <div class="landing">
    <header class="landing-header">
      <h1>Lacrima Videos</h1>
      <a href="/videos" class="landing-back">← Back to Lacrima Videos</a>
    </header>

    <main class="videos-doc">
      <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 20, 2026.</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains what data Lacrima Videos CLI (the "Tool") accesses, how it is used
        and stored, and how it can be deleted. The Tool is an internal application used only by the
        Lacrima Videos team to manage our own YouTube channels.
      </p>

      <h3>YouTube API Services</h3>
      <p>
        The Tool uses YouTube API Services. By using the Tool you agree to be bound by the
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
        Google's handling of data is described in the
        <a href="http://www.google.com/policies/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>
        (http://www.google.com/policies/privacy).
      </p>

      <h3>Data the Tool accesses</h3>
      <p>When a channel owner signs in with Google and grants access, the Tool can:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>upload videos and thumbnails to that channel and edit their metadata (title, description, tags, privacy and publication time);</li>
        <li>read the channel's basic information (channel ID, name, handle and public counts);</li>
        <li>read YouTube Analytics reports for that channel's own videos (for example views, watch time, average view duration, likes, comments, shares and subscribers gained or lost);</li>
        <li>read comments on the channel's own videos.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The Tool does not access any channel whose owner has not authorized it, and it never posts,
        comments or rates content on other channels.
      </p>

      <h3>How the data is used</h3>
      <p>
        The data is used only to publish our videos and to understand how they perform, so we
        can decide what to make next. We do not sell, rent or share it with third parties, and we do
        not use it for advertising.
      </p>

      <h3>Where it is stored</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>OAuth tokens</strong> are stored only on our own computer, in a file readable
          only by its owner. They are never sent to anyone other than Google.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Channel and video statistics</strong> are stored in our private database
          (hosted on Supabase), protected by access controls and accessible only to our team.
        </li>
        <li>
          Non-statistical data obtained from the API (such as titles or comment text) is refreshed or
          deleted within 30 days, as required by the YouTube API Services Developer Policies.
          Statistics are kept for up to 36 months to analyze trends.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>The Tool does not use cookies and does not collect any information from viewers of our videos.</p>

      <h3>Revoking access and deleting data</h3>
      <p>
        A channel owner can revoke the Tool's access at any time from the Google security settings page:
        <a href="https://security.google.com/settings/security/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://security.google.com/settings/security/permissions</a>.
        When access is revoked, or on request, we delete the stored token and all data obtained from that
        channel through the API within 7 days. To request deletion, write to
        <a href="mailto:lacrimadev@gmail.com">lacrimadev@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
      <p>If this policy changes, the "last updated" date will be revised.</p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this policy, you can reach us at
        <a href="mailto:lacrimadev@gmail.com">lacrimadev@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </main>

    <footer class="landing-footer">
      <p><a href="mailto:lacrimadev@gmail.com">lacrimadev@gmail.com</a></p>
      <p><a href="/videos">← Lacrima Videos</a> · <a href="/videos/terms">Terms of Service</a></p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
